solutions.explanation:
The fractions already have the same denominator, so subtract their numerators, keeping parentheses around the entire second numerator:
\[
\begin{aligned}
\frac{(2x^2-x)-(4+x)}{(x+1)(x-2)}
&=\frac{2x^2-2x-4}{(x+1)(x-2)}\\
&=\frac{2(x+1)(x-2)}{(x+1)(x-2)}.
\end{aligned}
\]
The numerator contains exactly the denominator as a factor. Because \(x\ne-1,2\), that factor is nonzero and can be canceled. The cancellation does not restore either excluded input. For every allowed \(x\), the expression equals \(\boxed{2}\), choice \(\boxed{\text{B}}\).
